<zk xmlns:n="native">
	<n:h1>WCAG 2.1 - 4.1.3 status messages</n:h1>
    <label multiline="true">
        1. open devtools and find #za11y-announcer, 
           it holds two regions: [role=log][aria-live=assertive] and [role=log][aria-live=polite]
        2. press "info" - a div reading "Info: Your changes have been saved." appears in the POLITE region
        3. press "warning" then "error" - those go to the ASSERTIVE region instead, prefixed "Warning: " / "Error: "
        4. type something that is not an e-mail address in the Email box, then click the page heading to blur it
           the errorbox opens AND the assertive region receives the constraint message, with no prefix
        5. in every case the notification and the errorbox themselves must have
           no role, no aria-live and no aria-label - announcing is the announcer's job
        6. with a screen reader on, steps 2 to 4 should be spoken without focus moving
    </label>
    <vlayout spacing="10px" hflex="1">
        <hlayout>
            <button id="info" label="info"
                onClick='Clients.showNotification("Your changes have been saved.", "info", null, null, -1, true)'/>
            <button id="warning" label="warning"
                onClick='Clients.showNotification("The system is busy.", "warning", null, null, -1, true)'/>
            <button id="error" label="error"
                onClick='Clients.showNotification("Could not reach the server.", "error", null, null, -1, true)'/>
        </hlayout>
        <hlayout>
            <label value="Email:"/>
            <textbox id="email" constraint="/.+@.+\.[a-z]+/: Please enter an e-mail address"/>
        </hlayout>
    </vlayout>
</zk>
